"Andrei's work at Fitbit centered on product design for wearables, specifically continuing the efforts from the Vector Watch acquisition, which focused on the intersection of hardware constraints and user interaction.

At UiPath, his role as Lead Product Designer shifted to agentic automation and AI-native systems. This represents a move from consumer hardware and software to more complex enterprise AI solutions, exploring how intelligent agents can integrate into workflows.

In essence, Fitbit was about refining human-computer interaction on a small, personal device, while UiPath is about designing the behavior and interaction of intelligent systems within larger digital environments.

Does this shift from wearables to AI automation resonate with your own interests? <suggestions>["Tell me more about the AI automation work", "What are the common threads across his work?"]</suggestions>"


